23201847,2026-06-14,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Problem caused by your funds being low,Overdrafts and overdraft fees,"I am filing this complaint regarding Citibanks handling of my Citi XXXX  Account and a disputed account offset. 

On or about XX/XX/year>, Citibank removed approximately {$300.00} from my Citi XXXX  Account ending in XXXX ( Account No. XXXX ) and applied those funds to a separate checking account with a negative balance. 

I do not believe this action was consistent with my understanding of the Citi XXXX Account product. My understanding is that the Citi XXXX Account is a basic banking account designed to limit overdraft-related issues. I do not understand why funds deposited into my XXXX Account were removed and applied to another account rather than remaining available in the account where they were deposited. 

In addition, Citibank is currently reporting my account balance as negative {$880.00}. I have not been provided with a clear explanation showing how this negative balance was calculated, what transactions caused it, or the authority relied upon to create or maintain this negative balance. 

I am requesting that Citibank provide : * The specific provision of the deposit agreement that authorized the transfer of funds from my Citi XXXX Account. 
* A complete transaction history and accounting showing how the negative balance of {$880.00} was calculated. 
* An explanation of the authority relied upon by Citibank to remove funds from my XXXX Account and apply them to another account. 
* A review of whether the offset and resulting account balance were applied correctly under Citibank policy. 
* Reimbursement of any funds that were removed or charged in error. 

Despite my attempts to obtain clarification directly from Citibank, I have not received a satisfactory explanation regarding either the account offset or the current negative balance. 

I respectfully request that the CFPB investigate this matter and require Citibank to provide a detailed written response. 

